{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/13","id":4502323907,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT3jXJs8AAAABDFwCww","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/13","diff_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/13.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/13.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/issues/13","number":13,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add native Berkeley DB packaging and combined-runtime qualification","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Preserve the full native MSYS LP64 Berkeley DB 6.2.32 recipe: C++, compatibility 1.85, DBM, static/shared libraries, all 15 utilities, and documentation.\n- Add source/payload provenance, narrow ARM64/libtool and upstream-test adaptations, and generation-bound ordinary native API/module evidence.\n- Reuse the existing working DB stage with the coherent combined runtime from crutkas/msys2-runtime#33; do not rebuild the DB payload or runtime.\n- Create genuine unsigned `db`, `libdb`, `libdb-devel`, and `db-docs` pacman-format archives. Validate every archive member, ALPM metadata, `.MTREE` path/size/hash association, and delivered PE as ordinary ARM64 (`0xAA64`).\n- Keep the MVP payload limited to two DB DLLs plus the license; retain the complete 5,605-file SDK stage separately.\n\n## Mutex timeout root cause and completed follow-up\n\nThe **original 900-second run failed** during configuration 9 of 24, with 83-created/76-recorded exit coverage. Its receipt and the original package/MVP limitation are preserved, not rewritten.\n\nThe unchanged full-load matrix subsequently **completed all 24 configurations naturally in approximately 3,734 seconds**, using a 7,200-second diagnostic bound: native CuTest exit 0, **314/314 processes observed**, no timeout and no nonzero native exits. That run retained the original **D70 runtime/DB cohort**, 2,000 iterations, process/thread counts, all three alignments, and code/data/unwind sections. Only output-path-dependent DWARF metadata differed in the rebuilt test worker.\n\nAn independent uncontended probe explains the elapsed cost: real DB yields requesting 1–2 microseconds took approximately **15.1–15.2 milliseconds**, as did direct `select` calls. Zero-yield remained about 0.0001 milliseconds. The same executable on combined907 reproduced the timing characteristic. The workload contains thousands of these sleeps, including a serialized wakeup thread; case durations scale with total lockers rather than alignment. No timer-resolution, mutex-barrier, scheduling-policy or workload change was made.\n\nThis resolves the retained timeout as an insufficient budget for this workload on the measured wait path, **not an observed alignment/ordering failure**. It does not prove the absence of every possible ordering bug, and **the D70 matrix is not a combined907 full-matrix or complete upstream-suite claim**. See `arm64-git-recovery/native/DB-MUTEX-TIMING.md` for raw per-case numbers, methodology and the implication for other microsecond-polling consumers.\n\n## Other evidence and boundaries\n\nThe combined907 C/DBM/1.85/process and ordinary C++ exception/module proof, supported utility paths, and load/verify/dump/reload round trip completed successfully. All four archives passed strict readback and independent `pacman -Qip` inspection. Target execution used the private native ARM64 runtime, not an x64 driver.\n\nThis PR does not claim signed repository/provider admission, a complete Perl/SSH/Git artifact, blanket SDK qualification, or optional Tcl coverage. No symlink-authorization or machine-settings workaround was performed. The unrelated binutils Texinfo fix is owned and independently validated on the toolchain PR; its success is not inherited as this PR's CI result.\n\nArtifact receipts remain outside Git. Only maintained code, fixtures, recipes, documentation and tests are committed. Historical producer-source snapshots preserve the exact bytes bound by earlier receipts.\n\n## Targeted controls\n\n`python -B -m unittest -q test_db_mutex_timing test_msys_library test_native_job_runner test_db_package test_pe_exports` — 58 passed.\n\nNegative controls reject mismatched proof inputs, modified continuation manifests, non-ARM64 payloads, invalid archive metadata, swapped mtree hashes, missing matrix cases, recycled process generations, wrong process images and nonzero raw exits.","created_at":"2026-09-11T03:44:29Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T08:11:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"828795ac24c6c32c9b236e812a05d4de4de28eb1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/13/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/13/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm